IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `il-interpretation-time`
IMPORT domain

-- g7-regulations.l4: sections 59 and 60 of the Regulation of Engagement in Work on Refrigeration or
-- Air-Conditioning Systems Law 5785-2025: the Minister's powers to set fees and to make regulations.
--
-- Written by ENCODER G7.  Imports only `prelude`, `daydate`, the vendored `il-interpretation-time` and `domain`.
--
-- Powers are encoded (the fleet lead's ruling 2, after the survey).  A power of the Minister is a regulative MAY
-- rule typed by who acts (`the Minister`) and what is done (set a fee by regulations; make regulations on a
-- matter), with its procedural preconditions, the approval of the Knesset Labour and Welfare Committee and the
-- consultation of another Minister, as computable conditions.  The CONTENT of a regulation is an input and
-- is never modelled here: the Fees Regulations are G8's, and no other regulation under sections 59 or 60 is in the
-- sources.  A rule that would need the content of a missing regulation returns a named REFUSE.
--
-- The powers are not gated on the commencement of the Law.  Section 63(a)(1) makes the commencement day depend on
-- the entry into force of the regulations under section 59, so the section 59 power has to be usable BEFORE the
-- commencement day, or the definition would be circular (see the note on the Interpretation Ordinance s.19 in
-- the time module's NOTES, fork F16, and fork F-R-3 in FRAGMENT-G7.md).
--
-- Not a period: nothing in sections 59 and 60 fixes a time for the Minister to act, so the rules carry no WITHIN.

§ `Chapter 7 — Miscellaneous provisions: fees and regulations (sections 59 and 60)`

§§ `The nouns of sections 59 and 60`

-- The "heads" of fee are the things section 59 lets the Minister set a fee FOR, one per "for" phrase of the
-- section: four in its first sentence and two more in its second, where a different rate may be set for a foreign
-- expert's temporary licence (section 9).  The survey counted five; the six constructors split the temporary licence
-- as the text does, an application or its renewal against the grant (fork F-R-1 in FRAGMENT-G7.md).
-- src:439 | {{ח:סעיף|59|אגרות}}
-- src:440 | {{ח:ת}} השר, באישור ועדת העבודה והרווחה של הכנסת, רשאי לקבוע אגרות בעד הגשת בקשה לרישיון, בעד מתן רישיון או חידושו, בעד בחינות הנדרשות לקבלת תעודת גמר ובכלל זה השגה על בחינות, ובעד השתלמויות לפי {{ח:פנימי|סעיף 17|סעיף 17}}; בתקנות כאמור רשאי השר לקבוע שיעורי אגרה שונים בעד הגשת בקשה לרישיון זמני למומחה זר או לחידושו לפי {{ח:פנימי|סעיף 9|סעיף 9}} ובעד מתן רישיון זמני כאמור.
-- src:441 | {{ח:ת}} {{ח:הערה|(פורסמו {{ח:חיצוני|תקנות הסדרת העיסוק בעבודה במערכת קירור או מיזוג אוויר (אגרות)|תקנות הסדרת העיסוק בעבודה במערכת קירור או מיזוג אוויר (אגרות), התשפ״ה–2025}}.)}}
@ref s.59 (src:439-441)
@desc A thing section 59 lets the Minister set a fee for; G8 consults the list for what a version of the Fees Regulations is silent on
DECLARE `Head of fee under section 59` IS ONE OF
    `a fee for submitting an application for a licence`
    `a fee for the grant of a licence, or for its renewal`
    `a fee for the examinations required for a final certificate, including an objection to an examination`
    `a fee for the continuing training under section 17`
    `a different rate of fee for submitting an application for a temporary licence for a foreign expert, or for its renewal`
    `a different rate of fee for the grant of a temporary licence for a foreign expert`

-- The matters section 60 lets the Minister make regulations on: the general power of paragraph (1), its three
-- named heads, and the two heads of paragraph (2).
-- src:444 | {{ח:ת}} השר ממונה על ביצוע חוק זה והוא רשאי –
-- src:445 | {{ח:תת|(1)}} באישור ועדת העבודה והרווחה של הכנסת, להתקין תקנות בכל עניין הנוגע לביצועו, ובכלל זה בעניינים אלה:
-- src:446 | {{ח:תתת|(א)}} דרישות הכשרה לשם קבלת רישיון, ובכלל זה השתתפות בהשתלמויות ועמידה בבחינות, ורשאי הוא לקבוע תנאים להכרה בהכשרה כאמור, את ההיקף הנדרש של שעות ההכשרה ותוכנה ותנאי הזכאות להשתתפות בהכשרה; בתקנות לפי פסקה זו רשאי השר לקבוע סוגים שונים של הכשרות לסוגי רישיונות שונים, לבעלי ניסיון קודם בביצוע עבודות מערכות קירור או מיזוג אוויר או לבעלי הכשרה קודמת בביצוע עבודות כאמור;
-- src:447 | {{ח:תתת|(ב)}} כללים בדבר בחינות הנדרשות לקבלת תעודת גמר, ובכלל זה השגה על בחינות אלה;
-- src:448 | {{ח:תתת|(ג)}} תנאים לשמש בודקים או מומחים לשם הסתייעות בהם לפי הוראות {{ח:פנימי|סעיף 34|סעיף 34}}, ובכלל זה תנאים לעניין השכלה, ניסיון מקצועי, התמחות והכשרה; תקנות לפי פסקה זו טעונות התייעצות עם השר הנוגע בדבר בהתאם לתחומי עיסוקם של הבודקים או המומחים;
-- src:449 | {{ח:תת|(2)}} להתקין תקנות בעניינים אלה:
-- src:450 | {{ח:תתת|(א)}} אופן הגשת בקשה לרישיון או חידושו, הפרטים שתכלול והמסמכים שיש לצרף אליה, ולעניין בקשה לחידוש רישיון – גם המועד להגשתה;
-- src:451 | {{ח:תתת|(ב)}} אופן הגשת בקשה לרישיון זמני למומחה זר או לחידושו, לפי {{ח:פנימי|סעיף 9|סעיף 9}}.
@ref s.60 (src:444-451)
@desc A matter on which section 60 lets the Minister make regulations; the first is the general power of paragraph (1) and the others its named heads
DECLARE `Matter of regulations under section 60` IS ONE OF
    `any matter connected with the implementation of the Law`                                     -- 60(1), the general power
    `the requirements of training for a licence`                                                  -- 60(1)(a)
    `the rules on the examinations required for a final certificate, including objections`        -- 60(1)(b)
    `the conditions for serving as testers or experts`                                            -- 60(1)(c)
    `the manner of applying for a licence or its renewal, and the time for applying to renew`     -- 60(2)(a)
    `the manner of applying for a temporary licence for a foreign expert, or for its renewal`     -- 60(2)(b)

@ref s.59 (src:439-441); s.60 (src:444-451)
@desc What the Minister does under sections 59 and 60: set a fee by regulations for a head of fee, or make regulations on a matter
DECLARE `Act of the Minister under sections 59 and 60` IS ONE OF
    `set a fee by regulations`
        HAS `the head of fee` IS A `Head of fee under section 59`
    `make regulations on a matter`
        HAS `the matter` IS A `Matter of regulations under section 60`

@ref s.59 (src:439-441); s.60 (src:444-451)
@desc The procedural facts that the Minister's regulations may depend on: the committee's approval and, for the testers and experts, the consultation of the Minister concerned
DECLARE `Procedure of the Minister's regulations` HAS
    `the Knesset Labour and Welfare Committee approved the regulations` IS A BOOLEAN @desc True if the Knesset Labour and Welfare Committee has approved the regulations (an input approval; the committee's own proceedings are outside the Law)
    `the Minister consulted the Minister concerned with the fields of the testers or experts` IS A BOOLEAN @desc True if the Minister of Labour consulted the Minister concerned, according to the fields of work of the testers or experts, as section 60(1)(c) requires of regulations under that paragraph

§§ `59. Fees`

-- 59.  The Minister, with the approval of the Committee, may set fees for the six heads above.
-- The text puts no figure and no deadline on the power.  The Fees Regulations that exercised it are G8's.
@ref s.59 (src:439-441)
GIVETH A LIST OF `Head of fee under section 59`
`s 59 — the heads of fee for which the Minister may set a fee` MEANS
    LIST `a fee for submitting an application for a licence`
       , `a fee for the grant of a licence, or for its renewal`
       , `a fee for the examinations required for a final certificate, including an objection to an examination`
       , `a fee for the continuing training under section 17`
       , `a different rate of fee for submitting an application for a temporary licence for a foreign expert, or for its renewal`
       , `a different rate of fee for the grant of a temporary licence for a foreign expert`

-- The second sentence: in the same regulations the Minister may set a different rate for the temporary licence of
-- a foreign expert (section 9): for the application or its renewal, and for the grant.
@ref s.59 (src:439-441)
GIVETH A LIST OF `Head of fee under section 59`
`s 59 — the heads of fee for which a different rate may be set for a foreign expert's temporary licence` MEANS
    LIST `a different rate of fee for submitting an application for a temporary licence for a foreign expert, or for its renewal`
       , `a different rate of fee for the grant of a temporary licence for a foreign expert`

@ref s.59 (src:439-441)
GIVEN head IS A `Head of fee under section 59`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 59 — the Law lets the Minister set a fee for` head MEANS
    elem head `s 59 — the heads of fee for which the Minister may set a fee`

@ref s.59 (src:439-441)
GIVEN procedure IS A `Procedure of the Minister's regulations`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 59 — the approval the Minister needs to set fees has been given` procedure MEANS
    procedure's `the Knesset Labour and Welfare Committee approved the regulations`

@ref s.59 (src:439-441)
GIVEN head IS A `Head of fee under section 59`
      procedure IS A `Procedure of the Minister's regulations`
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `Act of the Minister under sections 59 and 60`
`s 59 — the Minister's power to set a fee by regulations for` head `, given the procedure` procedure MEANS
    IF   `s 59 — the Law lets the Minister set a fee for` head
         AND `s 59 — the approval the Minister needs to set fees has been given` procedure
    THEN PARTY `the Minister` MAY `set a fee by regulations` head
    ELSE FULFILLED

§§ `60. Implementation and regulations`

-- 60 (lead-in).  The Minister is in charge of implementing the Law and may do what the paragraphs below say.
-- The first half is a statement of responsibility with no consequence of its own: carried as inert text.
-- The second half is the power, encoded paragraph by paragraph below.
@ref s.60 (src:444)
`s 60 — the Minister is in charge of implementing the Law` MEANS
    "Summary, not a quotation (the Hebrew above governs): the Minister is in charge of implementing the Law."

-- 60(1): with the approval of the Committee, regulations on any matter connected with implementation, including
-- the three heads (a) to (c).  60(2): regulations on two further matters, with no approval.  The two columns of
-- the table below are the whole of the difference between the paragraphs: where approval is required, and where
-- consultation is.
@ref s.60(1) (src:445); s.60(1)(a) (src:446); s.60(1)(b) (src:447); s.60(1)(c) (src:448); s.60(2) (src:449); s.60(2)(a) (src:450); s.60(2)(b) (src:451)
GIVEN m IS A `Matter of regulations under section 60`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 60 — the approval of the Knesset Labour and Welfare Committee is required for regulations on` m MEANS
    CONSIDER m
    WHEN `any matter connected with the implementation of the Law`                                  THEN TRUE   -- 60(1)
    WHEN `the requirements of training for a licence`                                               THEN TRUE   -- 60(1)(a)
    WHEN `the rules on the examinations required for a final certificate, including objections`     THEN TRUE   -- 60(1)(b)
    WHEN `the conditions for serving as testers or experts`                                         THEN TRUE   -- 60(1)(c)
    WHEN `the manner of applying for a licence or its renewal, and the time for applying to renew`  THEN FALSE  -- 60(2)(a)
    WHEN `the manner of applying for a temporary licence for a foreign expert, or for its renewal`  THEN FALSE  -- 60(2)(b)

@ref s.60(1)(c) (src:448)
GIVEN m IS A `Matter of regulations under section 60`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 60(1)(c) — consultation with the Minister concerned is required for regulations on` m MEANS
    CONSIDER m
    WHEN `the conditions for serving as testers or experts`                                         THEN TRUE   -- 60(1)(c)
    OTHERWISE                                                                                            FALSE  -- every other matter

@ref s.60(1) (src:445); s.60(1)(c) (src:448); s.60(2) (src:449)
GIVEN m IS A `Matter of regulations under section 60`
      procedure IS A `Procedure of the Minister's regulations`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 60 — the procedure required for regulations on` m `has been followed, given the procedure` procedure MEANS
        (    NOT `s 60 — the approval of the Knesset Labour and Welfare Committee is required for regulations on` m
         OR  procedure's `the Knesset Labour and Welfare Committee approved the regulations`)
    AND (    NOT `s 60(1)(c) — consultation with the Minister concerned is required for regulations on` m
         OR  procedure's `the Minister consulted the Minister concerned with the fields of the testers or experts`)

@ref s.60 (src:444-451)
GIVEN m IS A `Matter of regulations under section 60`
      procedure IS A `Procedure of the Minister's regulations`
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `Act of the Minister under sections 59 and 60`
`s 60 — the Minister's power to make regulations on` m `, given the procedure` procedure MEANS
    IF   `s 60 — the procedure required for regulations on` m `has been followed, given the procedure` procedure
    THEN PARTY `the Minister` MAY `make regulations on a matter` m
    ELSE FULFILLED

§§ `60(1) against 60(2): the general power and the specific matters (fork F-R-2)`

-- The matters of 60(2)(a) and (b), how to apply for a licence or a temporary licence, are also "matters connected
-- with the implementation" of the Law, which 60(1) lets the Minister regulate WITH the committee's approval.  Paragraph
-- (2) says the same matters may be regulated WITHOUT approval.  The text does not say whether the specific paragraph
-- displaces the general one for those matters or the general one still applies.  The reading taken is that the specific
-- paragraph governs (above).  The alternative: the general power covers every matter, so approval is required for all.
@ref s.60(1) (src:445); s.60(2) (src:449); s.60(2)(a) (src:450); s.60(2)(b) (src:451)
GIVEN m IS A `Matter of regulations under section 60`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 60 — reading paragraph (1) as covering the matters of paragraph (2), the approval of the Knesset Labour and Welfare Committee is required for regulations on` m MEANS
    -- every matter is a matter connected with implementation, so the general power of 60(1) reaches it
    TRUE

@ref s.60(1) (src:445); s.60(1)(c) (src:448); s.60(2) (src:449)
GIVEN m IS A `Matter of regulations under section 60`
      procedure IS A `Procedure of the Minister's regulations`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 60 — reading paragraph (1) as covering the matters of paragraph (2), the procedure required for regulations on` m `has been followed, given the procedure` procedure MEANS
        (    NOT `s 60 — reading paragraph (1) as covering the matters of paragraph (2), the approval of the Knesset Labour and Welfare Committee is required for regulations on` m
         OR  procedure's `the Knesset Labour and Welfare Committee approved the regulations`)
    AND (    NOT `s 60(1)(c) — consultation with the Minister concerned is required for regulations on` m
         OR  procedure's `the Minister consulted the Minister concerned with the fields of the testers or experts`)

§§ `60(2)(a). The time for submitting an application to renew (kind X: a length fixed by an official)`

-- A named refusal, returned and never stored.  No regulation under section 60(2)(a) is in the sources, so the time
-- for submitting an application to renew a licence is not known.  It is a length fixed by an official (kind X): an
-- input, never a default; the Law supplies none (compare section 8, which fixes the validity period and not the time to
-- apply for renewal).  Whether a regulation would count the time forward from a day (IL s.10(a)) or backward from the
-- end of validity (kind B, outside IL s.10) is not decidable until the regulation exists.
-- Once a regulation gives a nominal last day, the day is a deadline for doing something (or the end of a window for
-- an application), and the fleet lead's ruling 4 applies IL s.10(c) to it: a deadline does not end on a day of rest.
-- The days of rest are an input and are never computed.  The alternative without IL s.10(c) is the second function.
@ref s.60(2)(a) (src:450)
GIVEN a IS A TYPE
GIVETH AN a
`s 60(2)(a) fixes the time for an application to renew by regulations, and no regulation under section 60(2)(a) is in the sources` MEANS
    REFUSE "s 60(2)(a) fixes the time for an application to renew by regulations, and no regulation under section 60(2)(a) is in the sources"

@ref s.60(2)(a) (src:450)
GIVEN nominal IS A MAYBE DATE @desc The nominal last day for submitting an application to renew, as regulations under section 60(2)(a) give it for this licence; NOTHING if no such regulation applies or none is known
      calendar IS A `Calendar of rest days` @desc The days of rest, recess or holiday (input, never computed); used to move a nominal last day that falls on one
GIVETH A DATE
`s 60(2)(a) — the last day for an application to renew a licence` nominal calendar MEANS
    CONSIDER nominal
    WHEN JUST d
    THEN `s 10(c) — the last day of a period whose nominal last day is` d
             `, when days of rest, recess or holiday are`
             (`days of rest, recess or holiday listed in` (calendar's `days of rest, recess or holiday`))
    WHEN NOTHING
    THEN `s 60(2)(a) fixes the time for an application to renew by regulations, and no regulation under section 60(2)(a) is in the sources`

@ref s.60(2)(a) (src:450)
GIVEN nominal IS A MAYBE DATE @desc The nominal last day for submitting an application to renew, as regulations under section 60(2)(a) give it for this licence; NOTHING if no such regulation applies or none is known
GIVETH A DATE
`s 60(2)(a) — the last day for an application to renew a licence, IL s.10(c) not applied` nominal MEANS
    CONSIDER nominal
    WHEN JUST d
    THEN d
    WHEN NOTHING
    THEN `s 60(2)(a) fixes the time for an application to renew by regulations, and no regulation under section 60(2)(a) is in the sources`
